                <pb facs="0207" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg119"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports that Department’s telegram of the 10th has been complied
                    with, and that the Russian and Japanese ministers yesterday <pb facs="0208"
                        n="120" xml:id="pg120"/> handed declaration of war to the Chinese
                    Government, which will at once issue proclamation of neutrality.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
